# Chapter Pipelines

Follow `.claude/workflows/` for the task. Default for Book Two+: **lean pipeline**.

## Lean pipeline (`lean-pipeline.md`)

1. Select one writing agent (Carver / Hearthkeeper / Lyricist)
2. Prepare brief from outline, plan, characters, worldbuilding, style guide, convergence map
3. Append SDT checkpoint to every brief (see workflow)
4. Draft → `[book]/drafts/chapter-[NN]-draft.md`
5. Review in parallel: Unified Reviewer + Structure Reviewer + Voice Editor
6. Fan out per-character voice agents for every speaker (parallel)
7. Compile → `[book]/drafts/chapter-[NN]-revision-brief.md`
8. Update outline if new characters named (Character Name Rule)
9. Save canonical chapter → `[book]/chapter-[NN].md`

## Full pipeline (`chapter-pipeline.md`)

Use for major new chapters or when comparative drafts are wanted:

1. Writers' Room → 3 drafts + Editor's Table evaluation
2. Author chooses direction
3. All 8 review agents + per-character voice fan-out
4. Compile revision brief

## Writers' Room only (`writers-room.md`)

Three drafts + evaluation. Pause for author choice before review.

## Revision pass (`chapter-revision.md`)

Apply existing revision brief; re-run reviewers on revised chapter.

## Book-level review

- `lean-review.md` — consolidated 3 reviewers + voice fan-out per chapter
- `book-review-sonnet.md` — full 8 reviewers + voice fan-out

## Revision brief format

Sections: Critical Issues → Important Suggestions → Polish Notes → Voice Review (per-character) → Confirmed/Suspected Cross-Character Collapse → Strengths

Confirmed collapse = both characters' voice agents flag the same pair in the same scene.
